# Figma is the source of truth

Before changing layout, type, color, spacing, or images:

1. Load the Figma design-to-code skill.
2. Read the relevant frame(s) and variable definitions from the live file.
3. Use those values. Do not substitute nearby Tailwind defaults.

File: [Affordable Bellbottom Pier Drilling](https://www.figma.com/design/rNBkruQcCGz3s7uz1xn0bR/Affordable-Bellbottom-Pier-Drilling)

Known homepage frames (confirm in Figma if they move):

- Desktop: `5162:587` (1440 wide)
- Mobile: `5162:925` (400 wide)

Same token names can have different values on desktop vs mobile. Apply the value for the breakpoint you are implementing.

Do not invent a tablet layout. There is no tablet frame unless the user says they added one and gives the node. Until then, do not invent a middle breakpoint “from” desktop and mobile.

If the user points at a mismatch, read that section’s node. Do not guess which section they mean.
